===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*maþō}}, from {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*maþô}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*mat-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*mot-}}, used for insects and vermin. 

Cognate with {{cog|osx|maðo}} ({{cog|nl|made||maggot, worm}}), {{cog|goh|mado}} ({{cog|de|Made||maggot}}), {{cog|got|𐌼𐌰𐌸𐌰}}; Old Norse had the diminutive form {{m|non|maðkr}} (dialectal {{cog|en|mawk}}; compare also [[maddock]]). The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|xcl|մաթիլ||small louse}}.

